description: Every new runtime file, screen, and endpoint must have tests in the same change
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tests required

TDD (`tdd-enforcer`): write failing specs **before** runtime code. `passWithNoTests` is already `false` — do not add it.

| Change | Required tests |
|--------|----------------|
| API controller / validator | Vitest unit **and** Playwright `happy-path` + `failure-cases` |
| React component / hook | `tests/unit/` + Testing Library |
| UI screen | e2e-kit four files + smoke, happy-path, failure-cases, a11y, visual |
| `db-services` query | Unit test in that lib |
| Lib runtime | `libs/{name}/tests/unit/` |
| shadcn primitive in `shared-ui` | `libs/shared-ui/tests/unit/` covering public variants |

```ts
// BAD — only health e2e after adding POST /tenancy/pharmacies
test('health is mounted', async ({ request }) => { /* ... */ });

// GOOD — AC mapped
test('POST /tenancy/pharmacies returns 201 with tenant_id and location_id', async ({ request }) => { /* ... */ });
```

Forbidden: “tests later”, empty `tests/unit`, lowering coverage thresholds, widening `coverage.exclude` without review.
